{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>He enlarged Gad.</b> Meaning, HaShem enlarged for him with great possessions, as it is written (Numbers 32:1): ״וּמִקְנֶה רַב הָיָה [לִבְנֵי רְאוּבֵן] וְלִבְנֵי גָד״ and so forth. And the reason is as the verse stated there (Numbers 31:53): ״אַנְשֵׁי הַצָּבָא בָּזְזוּ אִישׁ לוֹ״, and since the children of Gad were mighty men of strength, they plundered more than all of them — and this is what Scripture appended to the statement ״He enlarged… as a lioness he dwells and tears prey״ and so forth."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:22:13.959899840Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}